  "unimplemented": {
    "open ends/world": "Overworld native fluid ticks, host replacement/collision/face support, source drain/renewal, placement, waterlogging, cauldrons/hives and spills are driven for contained fixtures. Other dimensions and entity/fire/candle workloads require additional contracts.",
    "spouts/drains": "Audited component-free tea/honey/chocolate recipes and ordinary buckets are driven. Component-bearing potions, sequenced assemblies, arbitrary recipes, block spouting integrations and native item entity flight need additional contracts.",
    "boilers": "BoilerData is source-audited through the tank water supply, the heat of the blocks under the tank (blaze burners, magma and lit campfires) and the engine/shaft pair; every engine drives a powered shaft at the boiler's efficiency and its stress capacity is observed.",
    "hoses/interfaces/effects": "World/entity/contraption callbacks absent.",
    "stored connection pressures": "The port retains endpoint pressures and flow paths, not stored Java PipeConnection pressures. Endpoint-path projections remain compared and are labeled in snapshots; pressure-only differences are not treated as port defects."
